# 18. KPI targets

## MVP KPIs

```
invoice extraction accuracy
number of invoices processed
number of exceptions detected
manual time saved
review turnaround time
duplicate invoices caught
missing contracts caught
```

## v1 KPIs

```
% invoices auto-classified
% invoices requiring human correction
average approval time
number of payment-risk issues detected
number of missing receipts detected
number of unpaid invoices detected
monthly close preparation time
```

## Suggested targets

```
80%+ invoices auto-readable
70%+ fields extracted correctly in first MVP
90%+ fields extracted correctly after correction/training
100% high-risk invoices routed to human review
0 automatic payments in v1
100% approval decisions logged
```

---

# 19. Guardrails

## Financial guardrails

```
No automatic bank transfers
No automatic tax payments
No automatic salary payments
No approval bypass
No payment without invoice file
No payment without vendor match
No payment if bank account changed without human confirmation
```

## Security guardrails

```
No secrets in Notion
No credentials in code
No shared personal logins where avoidable
Use 1Password or approved vault
Use minimum necessary permissions
Log all system actions
```

## Accounting guardrails

```
Money Forward remains source of truth
AI outputs are suggestions until approved
All exceptions remain visible until resolved
All corrections are logged
Human reviewer owns final decision
```

---

# 20. Final recommended execution order

The practical order for Mohamad should be:

```
1. Confirm first workflow: outsourced provider invoice verification
2. Collect 10–20 sample invoices
3. Map current manual process
4. Move credentials/secrets out of Notion
5. Build invoice extraction MVP
6. Add validation rules and exception flags
7. Add vendor/contract matching
8. Add reviewer approval and audit logs
9. Prepare Money Forward-ready data
10. Add reminders
11. Add expense reimbursement confirmation
12. Add outbound invoice support
13. Add bank sync monitoring
14. Add monthly close checklist
```

